From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:22:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/34] media: mediatek: seninf: Add MT6878 sensor interface
 driver

A driver for the sensor interface of the MT6878: CSI PHY 3.1 analog and
digital setup (efuse calibration, D-PHY 2/4 lanes and C-PHY 1..3 trios in
full-port mode, settle and trail timing), the CSI-2 MAC, the seninf
interface with its VC/DT filter, the seninf mux and the cam mux that feeds
a CAMSV tag, and the built-in test model as a test pattern control.

The hardware programming is ported from the MediaTek ISP7SP camsys driver
(mtk_csi_phy_3_1). The dynamic mux allocator of that driver is replaced by
a static route per CSI port, derived from the CAMSV engine linked in the
device tree. Every CSI port is a V4L2 sub-device with one sink and one
source pad, matched by the CAMSV notifier through its source endpoint.

DVFS, the timestamp recorder, frame sync, error detection, ULPS, init
deskew, LRTE, AOV, secure camera and debugfs are not supported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
